 extreme foreground, momentarily overlapping his navy jacket. He drops his hands and executes a sharp, forceful turn of his shoulders to the right, striking a dynamic, angular pose. His jacket flares out, revealing a neutral-toned t-shirt underneath. His gaze shifts away from the camera, looking off into the distance. The camera arcs right at a medium speed, tracking his rotation and capturing the shifting reflections of the city on the glass building behind him. [Shot 3] At 00:03.600, the camera cuts to a wide tracking shot positioned just above the pavement level. The man from Shot 1 strides purposefully forward along the grey concrete sidewalk. Clean, white typography reading \"AVAILABLE NOW\" scrolls vertically down the right side of the frame, weaving behind his swinging right arm to maintain the interlaced text aesthetic. The focus is directed toward the lower half of his body, highlighting the movement of his olive green cargo pants as they wrinkle dynamically. His heavy tan boots stomp rhythmically on the concrete. The camera pulls out at a fast speed, maintaining a constant distance just ahead of his advancing boots while the vertical grid lines of the skyscraper blur in the background.\noverall_soundscape: A faint, continuous urban hum of distant city traffic provides a subtle ambient baseline. A loud, resonant thud is heard prominently in the foreground as the heavy tan boot strikes the concrete pavement, followed by the crisp, audible rustle of thick cotton and denim as the man adjusts his cap. When the shot changes, a sharp, distinct swish of heavy fabric accompanies his sudden shoulder rotation. Finally, a rhythmic series of heavy, pronounced footsteps—thick rubber soles slapping firmly against the concrete—dominates the foreground, accompanied by the continuous, rough rustling of cargo pants.\nnon_diegetic_music: Electronic bass music, fast tempo, featuring a heavy, rhythmic drum machine beat, deep synthesizer drones, and sudden aggressive bass drops 